  so the other thing that i wanted to  mention which i think i had brought up  last video but not  tried yet was ring fit adventure it's an  exercising  action rpg on the switch that comes with  this circular band  thing uh that you have to move and i  will say that i think ring fit  because of the sense of resistance that  you get even from that band  probably was the most effective  workout that i got from any of these  unless i was like really trying hard  with uh racket or with fit xr because it  feels a little bit like having  more of a device for ring fit means that  you feel like you have to put more  strength into it whereas with the others  it's easier to just get  lazy and just like kind of sort of hit  stuff lazily you know  a lot better than i expected and i don't  know why i expected anything less  considering nintendo's history of  publishing pretty good fitness games  that is also a nice break from vr  because you can kind of only do so much  vr and of course not everyone has vr but  i feel like after a while like a vr  headset can start to hurt my head the  sweat like just feels gross because it's  on your face sometimes it feels a little  bit weird on your eyes ring fit removes  all of that  and will kick your butt in less than 10  minutes it's very very very good  i want to say thank you to all the  people who recommended it to me i'm a  really big fan so for anyone who's still  here i don't know  how many people are gonna make it this  far uh i wanted to talk about what we've  been doing with hashtag levelup2021.  essentially it's mostly on instagram  people are tagging me in their stories  and then i'm sharing them to try to get  encouragement  which i have 100 seen has encouraged  more people  to do these things so if someone's  working out they use the hashtag they  tag me and i share their story  i've had other people then say i saw you  sharing these stories and i decided to  jump on this train  and start working out and and getting a  walk in every day and i'm still seeing  people  every week be like hey i finally started  this alongside all of you and i think  that is  just the [ __ ] best just the coolest  that it's not just me who's doing it  it's everyone who's sharing it with me  that i can reshare and then  have a hundred thousand people see and  we just keep  increasing the cycle of people who are  trying to treat their bodies a little  bit better and get their bodies moving  so please keep doing that i really  appreciate it it's such a cool  way to like have this feel like a  community thing where you know every day  that someone tags me in a story  and i see it i go ah i wasn't going to  work out today  this person did i should and i'm also  getting ideas from the people who are  sharing this stuff the other thing that  i wanted to note  and i suggested this once before is  using my subreddit it's not mine it's  not official i do not mod it but it did  recently have a change in moderation  which makes me think that it is probably  a friendlier place than it was before so  if anyone wants to jump on the subreddit  which is uh  reddit.com alana pierce i  will also jump on there and talk to  people about this stuff  um specifically about level up 2021  about ideas about people  finding other video games that they can  suggest that can help people get fit  um anything along these lines i i really  want to encourage people to do  and i think it's a really cool community  effort for anyone who has been  joining so yeah everything's going very  slowly but well for me so far  very very slowly but i'm in good spirits  i'm healing that's the main thing but i  feel like i'm still on track  to get back into the very good shape  that i was in last year  alrighty i hope that this video was  useful to uh  anyone that it interested anyone  [Laughter]  i know fitness is a hard sell um but hey  you guys have been involved in this have  have made it easier for me so i really  appreciate that  thank you and i feel like you know maybe  when i'm back to the point that i want  to be at i'll post a before and after  picture  um but i do also try not to focus too  much on  how i look or like making it a negative  thing you know  try not to be like well this is the  before and the before is bad uh because  in my head it's just a change it's just  a different state of my  being so that is it for me today you  guys um i might do another one of these  updates probably not for a little while  maybe in a few months so if i'm like  back to where i want to be or if i've  learned anything new  this one just felt like because i had  actually you know made progress that i  should share huge thanks to raycon for  sponsoring this video check the link in  the description below to where you can  find out more from them and i will see  you guys next time  bye
 

